# Universal homeomorphisms as filtered colimits

A ring map which induces a universal homeomorphism on spectra is a filtered colimit of
finitely presented ring maps with the same property.

That statement is
`AlgebraicGeometry.isFilteredColimit_finitePresentation_universalHomeomorphism`.  It is proved,
together with its residue-field refinement
`AlgebraicGeometry.ind_finitePresentation_residueFieldMap_isIso_universalHomeomorphism`, with
the finite-stage criterion for universal homeomorphisms of affine schemes, and is re-exported
here.

